# AR landing CSS (buttons / pages QA)

Use skill **`auditing-landing-batch-pages-buttons`** + `run_batch_qa.py` for evidence. CSS-only unless the user asks for HTML.

## Do

- Solid primary fills: ensure AA (≥4.5:1). Mid-tone fills (`#059669`, `#0891b2`, `#0d9488`, …) + dark on-accent → **darken fill** and set on-accent / text to `#ffffff`.
- Per-variant hover `color` + `text-decoration: none` so global `a:hover` does not wash CTAs.
- Prefer `a.ctaClass:hover { … }` (no `!important`) after conflicting `a:hover` rules.
- Overflow: fix offenders (flex `min-width: 0`, honeypot clip). Confirm drawer still opens.

## Don't

- Blanket `.baseCta { color: #fff !important }` on shared base classes (breaks outline/ghost variants).
- White text on still-light primary (~3.5–4.4:1).
- `overflow-x: hidden` as the only `can_scroll_x` fix.
- Ship or claim done while contrast/visual JSON still has fails.
- Leave `/* QA-FIX */` or duplicate `!important` CTA appendages in production CSS.

## Done gate

`unique_btn_fails=0`, visual `page_fails=[]`, rtl clean, report synced when claiming batch QA complete.
